    "recommendations": "Based on the aerial observations provided, the following responder-safety recommendations are offered:\n\n• Mark each access point with a visible address identifier so responders can confirm which entrance they are using when approaching from different directions.\n\n• Mark the primary entrance distinctly from secondary access points to reduce approach confusion during emergency response.\n\n• Keep the internal drive aisle clear of parked vehicles and stored materials to allow emergency vehicles to move between structures without obstruction.\n\n• Keep the loading area clear of staged materials and equipment to preserve it as an emergency vehicle staging area.\n\n• Mark the path from each access point to the secondary building so responders can locate it quickly without prior site familiarity.\n\n• Post a site map at the primary access point showing the locations of both structures, the loading area, storage areas, and drive aisle routes.\n\n• Keep a clear travel path between the main building and secondary building free of stored materials or equipment.\n\n• Mark the outdoor storage area boundaries so responders can quickly identify where stored materials begin and end relative to the buildings.\n\n• Keep material storage positioned away from building walls and doorways to preserve access around all sides of both structures.\n\n• Mark the service area entrance with signage distinguishing it from the primary building entrance."
